# Casino API Test Cases

## 1. Login and Authentication

| ID | Test Scenario | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|
| TC-001 | Login with valid credentials | HTTP 200 is returned; the response contains valid access and refresh tokens. |
| TC-002 | Login with an incorrect password | Authentication is rejected; an appropriate error response is returned; no tokens are issued. |
| TC-003 | Login with a non-existent user | Authentication is rejected; an appropriate error response is returned; no tokens are issued. |
| TC-004 | Access a protected endpoint without a token | HTTP 401 is returned; protected resources are not accessed. |
| TC-005 | Access a protected endpoint with an invalid token | HTTP 401 is returned; the request is rejected. |
| TC-006 | Use an expired access token | HTTP 401 is returned; access is denied until a valid access token is obtained. |
| TC-007 | Refresh an access token using a valid refresh token | HTTP 200 is returned; a valid new access token is issued. |
| TC-008 | Refresh using an invalid refresh token | The refresh request is rejected; no valid access token is issued. |

## 2. Betting API

| ID | Test Scenario | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|
| TC-009 | Place a bet with valid data and sufficient balance | HTTP 200 is returned; a bet record is created; the wallet balance decreases by the bet amount; the response contains the expected bet details. |
| TC-010 | Place a bet with insufficient balance | The request is rejected; the wallet balance remains unchanged; no successful bet or debit transaction is recorded. |
| TC-011 | Place a bet with a negative amount | The request is rejected with a validation error; the wallet balance remains unchanged. |
| TC-012 | Place a bet with a missing amount | The request is rejected with a validation error; no bet is processed and the wallet balance remains unchanged. |
| TC-013 | Place a bet for a non-existent game | HTTP 404 is returned when consistent with the API specification; no bet is processed and the wallet balance remains unchanged. |
| TC-014 | Place a bet for an inactive game | The request is rejected according to the API's game-status rules; no bet is processed and the wallet balance remains unchanged. |
| TC-015 | Submit a bet with a mismatched user ID and JWT | HTTP 403 is returned; the request is rejected and the other user's wallet is not modified. |
| TC-016 | Submit a bet with a duplicate event ID | The duplicate request is rejected according to the API specification, such as HTTP 409; the original bet is not processed again and no additional debit occurs. |

## 3. Wallet and Database Validation

| ID | Test Scenario | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|
| TC-017 | Check wallet balance after a successful bet | The returned balance equals the initial balance minus the accepted bet amount, subject to the applicable business rules. |
| TC-018 | Check wallet balance after a rejected bet | The wallet balance matches the initial balance; no unintended debit is recorded. |
| TC-019 | Verify a successful bet in the database | Exactly one corresponding bet record exists with the expected user ID, game ID, amount, result, and event ID. |
| TC-020 | Verify transaction history | The transaction history contains the expected transaction records with correct amounts and transaction types. |
| TC-021 | Compare API balance with database balance | The API balance matches the corresponding database wallet balance after accounting for transaction completion and decimal precision. |
| TC-022 | Submit concurrent betting requests | Wallet balance and transaction records remain consistent; the balance does not become negative and no duplicate debit occurs. Requests that cannot be fulfilled are rejected appropriately. |

## 4. Event Processing and Webhooks

| ID | Test Scenario | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|
| TC-023 | Place a bet and verify the Kafka event | A corresponding Kafka event is published and can be consumed; its event ID and relevant bet details match the processed operation. |
| TC-024 | Send a webhook with a valid HMAC signature | The signature is successfully verified; the receiver accepts the payload for processing according to the webhook contract. |
| TC-025 | Send a webhook with an invalid signature | Signature verification fails; the webhook is rejected and the payload is not processed as an authenticated event. |
| TC-026 | Process the same event more than once | Duplicate processing is prevented according to the event-handling rules; no duplicate financial operation occurs. |

## 5. Performance Testing

| ID | Test Scenario | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|
| TC-027 | Run multiple concurrent API requests | The API handles the configured load within the predefined response-time and error-rate thresholds; unexpected failures are investigated. |
